# No secrets in git

Never commit tokens, API keys, passwords, or other secrets to git.

- Do not commit credential-bearing URLs (Cloud Agent `x-access-token` / `ghs_` tokens in remotes or `.beads/config.yaml` `sync.remote`).
- Prefer env vars (`GITHUB_TOKEN`, `LINEAR_API_KEY`, etc.) over storing secrets in tracked files.
- Scrub secrets before staging; if one was committed, rotate it and purge it from history.
